---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/img/selfie-creamcoat.jpeg';
---

<Layout
  title="About · Jessica Loredo"
  description="A product design leader fifteen years into K-12 edtech, most of the way through a counseling degree, working on how learning feels rather than how features behave."
>
  <section class="about">
    <header class="ab-head">
      <div class="ab-eyebrow">About</div>
      <h1 class="ab-title">Fifteen years designing learning products led me to a counseling degree</h1>
      <p class="ab-lede">That was not a career change. It was where the first thing kept pointing.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="ab-grid">
      <div class="ab-portrait">
        <Image src={portrait} alt="Jessica Loredo" width={760} />
        <p class="ab-caption">Kansas City, Missouri</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ab-prose">
        <p>
          I'm a product design leader with fifteen years in K-12 edtech, and I'm most of the way
          through a master's in counseling. I spent those years building products meant to help kids
          learn, and kept hitting the same wall: you can ship something well-researched,
          well-designed, and genuinely engaging, and still have no idea whether it reached anyone.
          The question of why kept leading somewhere product design doesn't go on its own, so I went
          and studied it.
        </p>

        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <p>
          I'm autistic and ADHD. In practice that means I read systems quickly and I'm pulled toward
          the parts everyone else routes around. When something is vague, I go in and stay there
          until it has a shape. Most of what's on this site started that way: an ownership question
          nobody could answer, a word every team used and no one had defined, a growth framework
          that didn't exist until it did.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work in a rhythm. Some days go deep, some stay light, and the deep ones are where the
          real work happens. That's partly how my brain runs and partly a conviction about the
          craft. We have tools that make us faster than we have ever been, which makes it more
          important, not less, to spend real time making sure we're building the right thing.
        </p>
        <p class="ab-pull">Speed is not the same as direction.</p>
        <p>
          Human-centered design only works if somebody is still doing the part where you go find out
          about the human. So the environments where I do my best work are flexible ones, with room
          for discovery and research and respect for the process. Give me that and an undefined
          problem, and I'll come back with something the whole team can point at.
        </p>

        <h2>What I'm after</h2>
        <p>
          I'm as good at solving something quickly as I am at sitting with it, and I've spent a long
          time being paid for the first one. What I want now is the second: strategy, systems, and
          work that changes how learning feels rather than how a feature behaves. That doesn't have
          to live on a screen. Some of the best interventions for how kids learn, and for how they
          feel while they're doing it, are programs and structures and rituals rather than products.
        </p>
        <p>
          I've led teams, and I care about the people on them getting better at their work. The
          growth framework on this site exists because I wanted the designers I worked with to be
          able to see themselves clearly, which is not something I could have faked caring about.
        </p>

        <h2>What I'm building toward</h2>
        <p>
          I'm finishing my counseling license and working toward a trauma-informed practice. I build
          things on the side, usually with whatever tooling is newest, because making something is
          the fastest way for me to understand it. I also paint, illustrate, and write, and I've
          stopped treating that as separate from the rest.
        </p>

        <p class="ab-contact">
          <a href="mailto:jessica@jessicaloredo.com">jessica@jessicaloredo.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 150px 48px 96px;
  }

  .ab-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
    max-width: 780px;
    margin-bottom: 64px;
  }

  .ab-eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  .ab-title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.8vw, 58px);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .ab-lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 24px);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--teal);
    padding-left: 20px;
  }

  .ab-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 320px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 72px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .ab-portrait {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    position: sticky;
    top: 108px;
  }

  .ab-portrait :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .ab-caption {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .ab-prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 22px;
    max-width: 640px;
  }

  .ab-prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .ab-prose p {
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .ab-pull {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.8vw, 30px) !important;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--ink) !important;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--teal);
    padding-left: 22px;
    margin: 6px 0;
  }

  .ab-contact {
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 0.5px solid var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .ab-contact a {
    color: var(--teal);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 0.5px solid var(--teal);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about { padding: 116px 24px 72px; }
    .ab-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; }
    .ab-portrait { position: static; max-width: 300px; }
    .ab-head { margin-bottom: 40px; }
  }
</style>
